# Live Compose stack — no recreate

You are attached to the **engine** service of the running
`aura-workbench_devcontainer` stack. Mutating that live stack hangs the agent.

## Forbidden (do not run)

- `docker compose … up` / `down` / `stop` / `restart` / `kill` on this project
- `--force-recreate`, volume renew, or any recreate of `engine` / `editor` /
  `imp-lab`
- Recreating containers “to pick up new mounts”

Do **not** probe or reproduce these hangs either.

## Required alternatives

- Sibling work: `docker compose … exec -T <service> bash -lc '…'`
- New mounts / `.env` path changes: ask the user to **rebuild/reopen**; do not
  recreate services
- Verify without a suitable running service: one-off `docker run --rm` with
  **host** bind mounts (see `scripts/run-*-windows-build.sh`)
- Image changes: `docker compose … build` is OK; do not recreate live containers
  to apply mid-session

Use `timeout` on non-trivial Docker CLI calls. Full detail:
[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) § Live Compose stack — hang avoidance.
